AB  - Architectural design requires knowledge and expertise in space planning, technical and cultural standards. Existing tools are either used to analyze designs that already exists, or to produce layouts without cultural context. This creates a disconnected workflow requiring iterative manual corrections. This paper introduces methodology Vastu Generative Framework (VGF) which is a hybrid Artificial Intelligence (AI) architecture that generates the Vastu compliant architectural plan directly from Natural Language input. The framework includes large language models (LLMs) on requirements extraction, a new Vastu Potential Map on how to convert the expression into continuous suitability landscapes, and a rule-based optimiser of Simulated Annealing to optimise both architectural and Vastu Shastra requirements constraints. Experiments with rectangular, L-shaped and triangular plots have proven that the maximum VGF complies between $85-94 \%$ with zero geometric overlaps where methods based on the baseline yield only between 15 45% compliance. The system produces production ready vector layouts at practical solve times ranging between 30 seconds to 90 seconds with a residential configuration. This means combining traditional's architectural wisdom with this modern, generative artificial intelligence technology; this transformative new workforce means that culturally aware design has become a reality for the user without needing technical expertise from this process or repeated iteration
ER  - 


