AB  - This paper studies power knowledge extraction technology, proposes a solution based on BERT model optimization, and integrates microservice architecture and knowledge service engine. By deeply integrating the ontology knowledge in the power field, the BERT model input layer is transformed, and the power semantic vector is constructed to realize multi-source knowledge fusion. In the experimental stage, a large-scale data set containing multi-source texts such as internal documents of power companies, public academic resources, and industry reports is constructed, with a total of about 50GB. After professional annotation, there are 70% training set, 15% validation set, 15% test set. Experiments are carried out to compare the performance of improved BERT model with traditional model fine-tuning and classical CRF algorithm. Results show that the improved BERT model achieves 92.5% precision, 91.2% recall rate and $91.8 \% ~\mathrm{F} 1$ value. The accuracy, recall rate, and F1 value increased 3.2%, 2.7% and 2.9% respectively compared with traditional large model. Compared with CRF algorithm, the improvement was significant at $10.5 \%, 9.8 \%, 10.1 \%$. The advantages are also obvious in the relationship extraction and attribute extraction tasks. The results of this study provide a new direction for the development of power knowledge extraction technology and strongly promote the intelligent development of power systems.
ER  - 


