AB  - Intelligent decision-making remains a major gap in traditional Business Process Management (BPM) systems, which are typically limited to rule-based workflows and require human intervention for complex decisions. This paper introduces LLMFlow, a novel low-code integration framework that connects large language models (LLMs), such as GPT-4, with the Microsoft Power Platform to deliver intelligent, end-to-end business process automation. LLMFlow was evaluated across three enterprise deployments: invoice processing, customer service automation, and supply chain optimization, achieving 92% processing accuracy, 62% faster response times, and 53% lower operational costs per transaction compared to traditional BPM solutions. The system sustained 132 requests per second, with a consistent average response time of 456 ms. To our knowledge, this work presents one of the early production-validated implementations of a multi-LLM orchestration framework that integrates predictive response-time routing with low-code workflow compilation and enterprise benchmarking.
ER  - 


