AB  - YogaWise is an adaptive and personalized yoga coaching tool combining computer vision techniques (posture recognition) with rule based methods to deliver coaching that is both safety oriented and directed toward a user's goals. As part of its decision-making process YogaWise uses criteria specific to each user (e.g., user's age, body mass index (BMI), health conditions, and fitness goals). This data is used to create userspecific yoga routines that eliminate postures that are inappropriate for the user. The posture recognition was performed using a convolutional neural network (CNN) based on VGG16 and the landmark detection (MediaPipe Pose) to identify the location of the user's joints. The geometry of the angles between the identified landmarks provide a basis for determining when a deviation occurs from the expected range of motion and provide instantaneous corrective feedback. The accuracy reached 96.2% for the training set and 94.5% for the validation dataset. The development of YogaWise utilised a software architecture consisting of a Python-based back-end and a React-based front end and demonstrated consistent reliability and practical usability in real-world yoga and wellness applications
ER  - 


